---
description: Image URL handling patterns for option images using the getOptionsImage utility to properly process relative paths from options.json and ensure Next.js Image component compatibility.
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---
- **Image URL Handling**
  - Always use `getOptionsImage` utility for option images from `options.json`
  ```typescript
  // ✅ DO: Use getOptionsImage for option image URLs
  import { getOptionsImage } from '@/lib/utils/get-options-image'
  
  <Image
    src={getOptionsImage(optionData.imageUrl)}
    alt={optionData.label}
  />
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Use raw image paths from options.json
  <Image
    src={optionData.imageUrl}  // This will fail for relative paths
    alt={optionData.label}
  />
  ```

- **URL Processing Rules**
  - All image paths in `options.json` should be either:
    - Relative paths from `app-images/placeholders/options/`
    - Full URLs (starting with http:// or https://)
  ```json
  // ✅ DO: Use relative paths or full URLs
  {
    "imageUrl": "bg-plain.jpg",           // Relative to options folder
    "imageUrl": "https://example.com/img" // Full URL
  }
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Use absolute paths or other formats
  {
    "imageUrl": "/images/bg-plain.jpg",   // Wrong path format
    "imageUrl": "public/images/bg.jpg"    // Wrong path format
  }
  ```

- **Implementation Details**
  - `getOptionsImage` handles:
    - Converting relative paths to full URLs via app-images API proxy
    - Preserving existing full URLs
    - Adding proper base URL from environment
    - URL encoding for special characters
  ```typescript
  // Example implementation
  getOptionsImage('bg-plain.jpg')
  // → '/api/app-images?path=app-images%2Fplaceholders%2Foptions%2Fbg-plain.jpg'
  
  getOptionsImage('https://example.com/img')
  // → 'https://example.com/img'
  ```

- **Common Issues**
  - Next.js Image component requires:
    - Absolute URLs (http:// or https://)
    - Paths starting with forward slash (/)
  - Raw paths from `options.json` will fail validation
  - Missing `getOptionsImage` will cause build/runtime errors

